3 CITY Ivančice
3 STAE South Moravian Region
3 CTRY Czech Republic
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The best known among Mendel's brothers is Simon, who at the age of 23 wrote a penitential poem, on the occasion of an epidemic that broke out among children in Vienna, in 1634. This poem passed through several edit
2 CONC ions, under the title "Mish'on (sic) la-Yeladim" (Support to Children), Frankfort-on-the-Main, 1711. The author died March 11, 1638, at Eibenschütz. The poem was printed by the grandson of the author, Meshullam Solomon Fischhof, w
2 CONC ho added a commentary, "Rab Shalom" (Much Peace). He also published several prayers and hymns of Israel Nagara, with additions of his own (Frankfort-on-the-Main, 1712).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=2108&letter=A
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Grabschriften des Alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien" Band I, by Dr. Bernhard Wachstein-pg. 329 (no. 429) 
2 CONT
2 CONT died young
