1 NAME Judah "The younger" /Wahl Katzenellenbogen/ [ances. of Mendelssohn]
2 GIVN Judah "The younger"
2 NSFX [ances. of Mendelssohn]
2 _MARNM Wahl Katzenellenbogen
2 NICK Simeon
1 NAME יהודה /ואהל קצנלנבוגן/
2 GIVN יהודה
2 SURN ואהל קצנלנבוגן
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1600
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1644
1 OCCU Rabbi
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} REPLY to REPLY to TEMPORARY POST:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) According to the 3rd Edition of Unbroken Chain, Chapter 3, page 430:
2 CONT
2 CONT G5.5 Judah Wahl, called the "younger," as he was named after his deceased brother, married Dreizel, daughter of Simeon Wulff of Vilna, who settled in Hamburg and died in 1682. Judah and Dreizel were distantly related by virtue of 
2 CONC the fact that his maternal grandmother, Miriam was a sister of Simeon Wulff's ancestor, the prominent Talmudist R. Moses Isserles, known in the rabbinical world as the ReMa 1520-72 of Cracow, where the family originated. Dreizel t
2 CONC he elder was the wife of R. Simha Bonem Meisel (Meisels) of Cracow.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) According to page 26 of the current edition of UC, we find the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT G5.6 Judah Katzenellenbogen, known as "the younger", was the son from the 2nd wife.  He married the daughter of R. Zeev Wolf, son of R. Isaac Bonem's of Vilna.  R. Zeev's mother was the daughter of R. Simcha Bones Meisels of Craco
2 CONC w, son-in-law of R. Moses Isserles (the ReMa).
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on the above and the GENI tree, there are two ways of reconciling these facts: 1) It could be that https://www.geni.com/people/Hinda-Katzenellenbogen/6000000007677455945 is the second wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabb
2 CONC i-Meir-Wahl-Katzenellenbogen-MaHaRash/6000000000348786317, and the mother of https://www.geni.com/people/R-Judah-Wahl-Katzenellenbogen-ances-of-Mendelssohn/6000000000938774161, or 2) it could be that https://www.geni.com/people/%D
2 CONC 7%94%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%AA-%D7%91%D7%99%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%94-%D7%95%D7%95%D7%90%D7%94%D7%9C-%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%A0%D7%9C%D7%A0%D7%91%D7%95%D7%92%D7%9F/6000000028022930885 is the second wife, and the mother of https://www.geni.com
2 CONC /people/R-Judah-Wahl-Katzenellenbogen-ances-of-Mendelssohn/6000000000938774161?through=6000000007677455945.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the locked (and therefore presumably vetted) GENI profile of https://www.geni.com/people/Hinda-Katzenellenbogen/6000000007677455945, she is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Pinchas-HaLevi-Horowitz/338
2 CONC 1543?through=6000000007677455945 and https://www.geni.com/people/Miriam-Beila-Horowitz-Isserles-REMA-s-sister/6000000000938419938, and therefore the sister of ReMa. 2) https://www.geni.com/people/%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%
2 CONC AA-%D7%91%D7%99%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%94-%D7%95%D7%95%D7%90%D7%94%D7%9C-%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%A0%D7%9C%D7%A0%D7%91%D7%95%D7%92%D7%9F/6000000028022930885 is shown as the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/rabbi-nachum-A-B-D-ludmir/60000001
2 CONC 73470538476?through=6000000028022930885 (a fact which is confirmed by the Volodymir Book (https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/Volodymyr_Volynskyy/vol022.html#Page25), with no mother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Since I see no evidence that https://www.geni.com/people/%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%AA-%D7%91%D7%99%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%94-%D7%95%D7%95%D7%90%D7%94%D7%9C-%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%A0%D7%9C%D7%A0%D7%91%D7%95%D7%92%D7%9F/6000000028022930885
2 CONC  is the daughter of ReMa's sister, it seems that option 1 is the best way of reconciling the two UC statements:. https://www.geni.com/people/Hinda-Katzenellenbogen/6000000007677455945 is the second wife of https://www.geni.com/peo
2 CONC ple/Rabbi-Meir-Wahl-Katzenellenbogen-MaHaRash/6000000000348786317, and the mother of https://www.geni.com/people/R-Judah-Wahl-Katzenellenbogen-ances-of-Mendelssohn/6000000000938774161. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Since there is room for confusion based on the UC 3rd Edition, I think it wise to retain the 'TEMPORARY' posts and REPLIES.
2 CONT
2 CONT REPLY to TEMPORARY POST:
2 CONT In page 26 of the current edition of UC, we find the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT G5.6 Judah Katzenellenbogen, known as "the younger", was the son from the 2nd wife.  He married the daughter of R. Zeev Wolf, son of R. Isaac Bonem's of Vilna.  R. Zeev's mother was the daughter of R. Simcha Bones Meisels of Craco
2 CONC w, son-in-law of R. Moses Isserles (the ReMa).
2 CONT
2 CONT Since the 2nd wife is listed as Beila (see Chapter 1, page 23), doesn't this mean that Beila should be the correct mother?
2 CONT
2 CONT TEMPORARY POST: The correct mother of Judah the Younger is: 
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Hinda-Katzenellenbogen/6000000007677455945
2 CONT Please detach him from https://www.geni.com/people/%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%AA-%D7%91%D7%99%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%94-%D7%95%D7%95%D7%90%D7%94%D7%9C-%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%A0%D7%9C%D7%A0%D7%91%D7%95%D7%92%D7%9F/6000000028022930885 and a
2 CONC ttach him to Hinda (keeping the father the same: he was married twice).
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the 3rd Edition of Unbroken Chain, Chapter 3, page 430:
2 CONT
2 CONT G5.5 Judah Wahl, called the "younger," as he was named after his deceased brother, married Dreizel, daughter of Simeon Wulff of Vilna, who settled in Hamburg and died in 1682. Judah and Dreizel were distantly related by virtue of 
2 CONC the fact that his maternal grandmother, Miriam was a sister of Simeon Wulff's ancestor, the prominent Talmudist R. Moses Isserles, known in the rabbinical world as the ReMa 1520-72 of Cracow, where the family originated. Dreizel t
2 CONC he elder was the wife of R. Simha Bonem Meisel (Meisels) of Cracow.
2 CONT
2 CONT The reference cited on the https://www.geni.com/people/%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%AA-%D7%91%D7%99%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%94-%D7%95%D7%95%D7%90%D7%94%D7%9C-%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%A0%D7%9C%D7%A0%D7%91%D7%95%D7%92%D7%9F/6000000028022930885?t
2 CONC hrough=6000000000348786317 page,  from the Volodymyr Book (https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/Volodymyr_Volynskyy/vol022.html#Page25) says that https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Meir-Wahl-Katzenellenbogen-MaHaRash/600000000034878631
2 CONC 7 was married to Bielah but not that she was the mother of Judah the Younger. The UC passage quoted above says that Judah's maternal grandmother was Hinda's mother Miriam. 
2 CONT (01 OCT 2022)
2 CONT
