1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from Chortkov; son Meir Horowitz & daughter Katz
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Zvi Hirsch Horowitz, ABD Czortkow from 1726 until his death in 1754.  He married the daughter of R. Mordecai, son of R. Zvi Hirsch, son of Zechariah Mendel.  
2 CONT
2 CONT They had eleven children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He wrote an approbation to "Bracha Abraham".
2 CONT
2 CONT He was greatly respected by the Best (Baal Shem Tov), his master, who declared that he was one of three families in Israel who gave more respected sons to the rabbinical calling than any other; namely Rabbi Samuel Shmelke of Nikol
2 CONC sburg and Rabbi Pinchas of Frankfurt who were disciples of Dov Ber, the successor of the Besht.
2 CONT
2 CONT Once when the two sons returned home from their studies under the Maggid, their father inquired of them what they had learned.
2 CONT
2 CONT "We have learned belief that the soul is the kernel and the body its shell," was their reply.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although late eighteenth and early nineteenth century Germany was the hearland of Chassidic opposition, yet two Chassidic sons of this scholar were elected Av Beit Din of German cities - Frankfurt and Nikolsburg.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The story is related that these posts were due to the influence of Mayer Amschel Rothchild  (father of the five famous brothers), who as a young man, had been a sexton in the study house of R. Zvi Hirsch Horowitz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>><nowiki>------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT  The young community of [http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/chortkov/cho031.html  Chortkov] earned a name for itself when [http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/chortkov/cho031.html  Rabbi Zvi Hirsh Horovitz], who is known even today by th
2 CONC e name Rabbi Reb Hirsheli, was hired to be her rabbi and educator. He was considered, together with Rabbi Segal from Lvov ,and the Rabbi from Stanislave, to be the Gaon (genius) from Podolia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Chortkov's religious school, came many genius rabbis who serve many large communities in the west. Among them were the two brothers, Rabbi Smuelike and Rabbi Pinchas, sons of the righteous rabbi, Rabbi Hirsheli from Chortkov.
2 CONC  His students worked as teachers and instructors in the important communities of Nikelshborg in Moravia, and Frankfurt on Main, which was a very important and large Ashcenazi community of that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://www.microtarget.com/HorowitzAssociation/Horowitz%20Rev.5.1.pdf  Horowitz Family Alliance Rabbinical Branches Tree]
2 CONT
