1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Several sources give R' Aryeh Leib Fraenkel-Teomim's death year as 1773 in Leipnik, Moravia.  However, given that a grandson born c1740 was named in his honor, his death clearly occurred sometime prior to that chil
2 CONC d's birth.  He was A.B.D. first in Kreshinov, then later in Leipnik.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Familie Teomim", by Leopold Lowenstein:  "Arje Lob, rabbi in [Krzeszow] and Leipnik, whose son Josef (died 1782) was rabbi in Ostrawze, Opatow, Poznan and Lublin (his wife was the daughter of R. Natan Nata in Turbin and grand
2 CONC daughter of R. Baruch Rapoport in Furth). One son of this Joseph was R. Arje Jehuda Lob, rabbi in Brody...; Another son was Saul Feibel, who later followed his father as a rabbi in Ostrawze, whose famous son R. Baruch Teomim Frank
2 CONC el was a rabbi in Wischnitz and Leipnik, where he died on 7 Tamus (June 19) 1828. The works written by R. Baruch are: Glossen zur Mischna... He was married in the first marriage to a daughter of Rabbi Jehuda Parnes von Wischnitz a
2 CONC nd in second marriage to the daughter of R. Zbi Josua Horwitz... The children of R. Baruch Teomim were Josua Heschel, rabbi in Komorn, and a daughter, wife of R. Chajjim Halberstamm, rabbi in Zans.
2 CONT
