1 OCCU Drucker, Vorsinger / Schächter
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Printer in Sulzbach from 1764 to 1771
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.rijo.homepage.t-online.de/pdf/EN_BY_JU_sulz.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.alemannia-judaica.de/sulzbach-rosenberg_synagoge.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Name change in 1813:
2 CONT
2 CONT •Der von allen Söhnen Ahrons angenommene Familienname Arnstein ist eine Zusammensetzung aus "Ahron" und der bei Familien- namen beliebten Bildungssilbe "-stein". Naftalis Nachkommen benützen die Bildungssilbe "-berger" zu Neftelbe
2 CONC rger
2 CONT
2 CONT see: [http://www.archive.org/stream/charlesperrystanton_04_reel04#page/n886/mode/1up Charles Perry Stanton Papers ar 25138]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Naftali continued to wander around the world and provided auditor and Mining positions in Würzburg and Fulda 30 years later, the 70-year-old reappeared in Sulzbach and his son Wolf Hirsch Naftali appeared after him.
2 CONT * the poor 70-year-old man was advised to assert his ius alimendi in Franconia. The community of Sulzbach consisted almost entirely of beggars anyway. His children and relatives stepped in with unanimous honor for him and declared
2 CONC  their solidarity for the future to take over his entertainment to the fullest.Then the official residence permit came on January 18, 1811.
2 CONT * In addition to Seckel, the certificate issued is signed by Naftali's son Wolf Hirsch Naftali, whose son-in-law Abraham Moises Löb the nephew Naftalis and Ahron's sons Joseph Ahron Haium Ahron u Löb Ahron by Raphael Aisak, appare
2 CONC ntly the son of Jsak Raphael of a son-in-law Salman, and 2 nephews are also mentioned Feist Schlenker and Mos Engländer both likely to have sons-in-law Ahrons Feist Veit Schlenker is described in a previous report by the Sulzbach 
2 CONC district court in 1802 as a man of skillful head and feather entrusted with the remuneration of goods see also III No 54
2 CONT
2 CONT * He had three Wives
2 CONT * Children from all three wives  (He left daughters twice based on the book and we know of Wolf Hirsch Naftali)
2 CONT * Naftali Salomon Left Sulzbach after 2nd wife death, Came from or went to this location: Reichsdorf Gocksheim
2 CONT * Third wife is Eva and we are making the assumption that is Wolf Hirsch Naftali's mother.
2 CONT  * Seligman Lazarus, the guardian of Naftali's daughter from his first marriage Reference: https://books.google.com/books?id=CiVNAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA83&dq=naftali+sulzbach&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiowYikkejnAhWT9Z4K
2 CONC HeCzCUgQ6AEwAXoECAUQAg#v=onepage&q=naftali%20sulzbach&f=false
