2 TITL Hesped
2 NOTE A few years prior to his passing, R' Chanoch Heinich moved to Khruli. He was already an elderly man, so journeying such a distance to resettle seems odd.
3 CONT
3 CONT I hypothesise that as Napoleon begun his invasion, it was no longer safe for him to remain. We can take a parallel from the Alter Rebbe of Liadi who also fled Napoleon's invasion.
3 CONT
3 CONT Further, Khruli might seem inaccessible for a man of his age to travel to. But on careful aerial observation one will notice that the Dnieper River runs down the east side of Shklov, in the very near vicinity - and snakes its way 
3 CONC down a very reasonable marine route that passes to the west side of Khruli. It is highly probably that the elderly R' Schick was able to make a rapid escape from Shklov via a boat!
3 CONT
3 CONT But why Khruli? The only link I have found so far is that the Rav of Khruli had previously been Rav in a town north of Shklov very closeby. It is entirely likely that Rav Schick and this Rav were already acquainted and this is how
3 CONC  the offer of refuge in Khruli came to be.
