2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT <p>Our most famous ancestor. A member of the well known and documented Horowitz (Levite) Family.. Rabbi Reb Shmelke Horowitz was (together with his brother Rabbi Pihas Horowitz (author of "HaFlah") a disciple of Rabbi Dov Beer - t
2 CONC he Maggid of Mezritch and the senior propagator of Hasidism. He and the Flah studied in non-Hasidic "lihuanian" yeshivot but after meeting the Maggid, became his ardent followers. He served first in Richwal and Shiniava and was el
2 CONC ected in 1773 as Chief Rabbi of Nikolsburg in Moravia (today Mikulov in the Check Republic) where he created a major Yeshiva that attracted outstsanding students -themselves future senior hasidic masters (see short list in Notes, 
2 CONC Citation Note 1 page 29). Most books on Hasidism mention him and his teachings (See a short bibliography in Notes, Citation Notes).</p>
