2 CONT G7. R. Moses, who as a young man first studied under his grandfather, R. Heschel, in Brest, where he later established his own yeshiva.  He was the author of noveliae, ''Tiferet LeMoshe'', published by his grandson in 1776 at Berl
2 CONC in; and also ''hagalot'' (glosses) on the Talmud in 1673.  He was ABD Grodno and signed  at the meeting of the Four Lands at Zulz (1673), Zablodov (1676), Chomsk (1679) and Leczna (1681).  He wrote approbations to ''Migdal David''
2 CONC  in 1674 at Grodno, and ''Kench Chochma'' in 1679 at Chomsk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (3rd Edition) Volume 3, Chapter 9, page 698
