3 STAE Lviv Oblast
3 CTRY Ukraine
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Die Familie Teomim", by Leopold Lowenstein:  "Meir Teomim, learned preacher in Lubartow and Lemberg, author of [H.W.] (Zolkiew 1746) and [H.W.] (Frankfurt am Main, 1782). When he was four years old, he lost his pa
2 CONC rents and was brought up in the house of his uncle R. Elia R. Arons; he died in Lviv in 1775. [H.W.] was also repeatedly repeated Talmudic novellas by his son Josef (No. X)."
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born about 1703, the son of Joseph Samuel Teomim-Frankel (c1681-c1707).  He was named in honor of his paternal grandfather, R' Yitchok Meir Teomim-Frankel, aka "Dr. Markus Fraenkel", who died in Zolkow in 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT A footnote in the Lowenstein summary confirms that he was the son of Joseph Teomim:  ".... Meir ben Josef Teomim. that [H.W.] written by his son Josef - As the death date of R. Meir b. Josef Teomim is specified by Buber of the 19 
2 CONC Tamus 533 (i.e. 10 July 1773) (likewise also through and Gruber II, No. 31, p. 97); in the journal [H.W.] 1869, p. 285 Monday, 19 Tamus 530; However, since this day did not fall on a Monday in either 530 or 533, the year 531 seems
2 CONC  to be the correct one and R. Meir Teomim died on Monday 19 Tamus 531 (July 1, 1771), with the approval of his son Josef [Hw] of 2 Nissan 532, in which the father is described as dead.
