1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samson_Wertheimer
2 CONT
2 CONT Samson Wertheimer's second son, Löb, married a daughter of Issachar ha-Levi Bermann of Halberstadt, a relative of Leffman Behrens, court Jew of Hanover; thus the three great "shetadlanin" were closely connected. Samson's sons-in-l
2 CONC aw were: R. Moses Kann of Frankfurt-on-the-Main; Issacbar Berush Eskeles, father of the Vienna banker Bernhard Eskeles; Joseph, son of R. David Oppenheimer; and Seligmann Berend Kohn, called Solomon of Hamburg. His youngest son, J
2 CONC oseph Josel (b. 1718), married a daughter of his stepbrother Wolf. Joseph died in Vienna (1761), where he was reportedly greatly esteemed for his charity and Talmudic learning.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Better known as (just) Loeb (Löb)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Familie Wolf" - by Ernst Wolf 1924 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.fpe.ch/stammbaum/ see pg. 118 
2 CONT
2 CONT see also chart Lion Gomperz. & Family Latzko
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Grabschriften des Alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Band II -by Dr. Bernhard Wachstein- no. 958
