1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The yizkor (memorial) book for Kamien-Koszyrski (1965) says (in translation):
2 CONT
2 CONT "... Kamen-Kashirskiy was in the care of Kovel's Rabbi Ya'acov Arieh. The Rabbi of Kovel, about 150 years ago, had two sons and two daughters. One of the sons served as the Rabbi of Stobykhva [R' Israel], while the second, Rabbi L
2 CONC evi Yitzhak, served as Rabbi to Kamen-Kashirskiy."
2 CONT
2 CONT An article in Kowel: sefer edut ve-zikaron le-kehilatenu she-ala aleha ka-koret about HaZaken miNeskhiz identifies his daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT - the first daughter, Gitele, wife of R' Menachem-Monish Marguliot, son of R' Chaim Mordechai Marguliot.
2 CONT
2 CONT - the second, Rikele, wife of the Magid haGadol of Trisk, R' Abraham (Magen Avraham), son of R' Mordechai or Tshernobil, son of R' Nahum or Tshernobil. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * for Rikel Twersky, wife of R' Avrum Twersky of Trisk, see http://www.geni.com/people/Rikel-Twersky/6000000006712075217
2 CONT
2 CONT Leoni, in "HaZaken miNeskhiz" says (in translation): "The second son [of R' Mordechai] was haRav haGaon R. Jacob Aryeh, known as 'haRav miKovli' ... . ... grandfather of Jacob-???, son of the Maggid of Trisk."
