1 NOTE {geni:about_me} An article, "History of the Jews of Volhyn" in Pinkas hakehillot Polin (1990), says (in translation):
2 CONT
2 CONT "Another Hasidic dynasty was that of Nezkizh, founded by Rabbi Mordecai Shapira (1748-1800) who was one of the disciples of Yehiel Mikhal of Zlotchov. He was a 'miracle-worker' and his sayings were collected in the book Rishfe Eis
2 CONC h [Sparks of Fire]. His first-born son, Rabbi Ya'akov Arieh (1780-1830) lived in Kovel, Nezkizh and Trisk. His son born to him in old age, Rabbi Isaac (1789-1868), was a disciple of Rabbi Barukh of Miedzyboz and of the Seer of Lub
2 CONC lin [Ya'akov Yitzhak d. 1815]. He was influenced by Rabbi Yitzhak Levi of Berdichev and like his father was a 'miracle-worker.' He was the author of Toldot Yitzhak [The Generations of Isaac] and Zikhron Tov [Good Memory]. Descenda
2 CONC nts of this dynasty spread to Kovel, Ostila, Stovikhova, Poryck and other places."
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Dynner, Men of Silk: his second wife was "the daughter of the zaddik Levi Isaac of Berdyczow,"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-455098731-1-501843/itzhak-shapira-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-8e4e696b0d8c6ac05840f75d9bfaddd6&mrid=6282bed3cd299e330594fb30939447f2 MyHeritage Fam
2 CONC ily Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 14 2021, 0:52:34 UTC''
