1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Phineas (Pinchas) Katzenellenbogen succeeded his father as A.B.D. of Ettingen where he remained for some fifty years, and died there. He was buried in Wallerstein.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many of his letters of correspondence to his father in Ettingen, written while in Schwabach, are found in manuscript at Oxford.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Esther, the daughter of Judah Leib Lemberger (Lwow), A.B.D. Schwabach (from 1780 - 1792) and of Ansbach (see chapter 111 - Lwow family).
2 CONT
2 CONT The silver cup of the Chevra Kadisha of Schwabach, to be seen in the Jewish Museum,. Jerusalem, has an inscription dated 1791 which states: "A.B.D. Judah Leib Lwow, long may he live ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (1990) Volume 1, Chapter 11, page 99, G 10.2
