2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nathan_Nata_Spira  '''Nathan Nata Spira]( נתן נטע שפירא‎; 1585 – July 20, 1633) was a Polish rabbi and kabbalist. He had an important role in spreading Isaac Luria's teachings throughout Poland. Spira
2 CONC  was the author of the Megaleh Amukot.  Spira was a student of Meir Lublin.
2 CONT Spira descended from a rabbinical family, which traced its lineage as far back to Rashi, the noted 11th century French commentator. He was named after his grandfather Nathan Nata Spira, who was rabbi in Hrodna and authored of Mevo
2 CONC  Shearim (1575) and Imrei shefer (1597).  His father was Solomon Spira.
2 CONT Spira had seven children, three sons and four daughters. Spira was Chief Rabbi of Kraków, but refused a salary.
2 CONT Author of [Megale Amukos מגלה עמוקות http://www.hebrewbooks.org/33146]
2 CONT
