1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There is a lot of confusion regarding This Rebetzen Pesel.
2 CONT
2 CONT If she was a brother of Reb Shmelke M'nikelsburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to our Uncle (Reb Shlomo Fructher) in his Sefer "Egereth Shlomo" (Jerusalem, 1960). she was a sister, But others argue that this is impossibale because of a few reasons.
2 CONT
2 CONT We would appreciate if we can get some more information on that.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please email me @ adardesign@gmail.com.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks Much  
2 CONT
2 CONT Please look at the profile photo. According to ספר צרור החיים of her son Reb Shmelka of Selish (printed 1875), Pessil was the daughter of Brandel. Brandel was the sister of Reb Shmelka of Nikulsburg. Brandel's husband was Yechiel 
2 CONC Halpern.  
2 CONT
2 CONT It also can't be that Pessil was born Circa 1740. Her son Reb Shmelka of Selish was born in 1804. That makes her 64 years old when he was born. Also, Pessil's mother Malka was born Circa 1680 which makes her 60 years old when Pess
2 CONC il was born. Both dates are very off. Pessil was for sure not the daughter of R' Tzvi Hirsch of Chortkov, and she was surely born after 1760, which makes it impossible for her to be the mother of the 3 brothers, Fruchter, Adler an
2 CONC d Stern, since they were born between 1752 - 1762
