1 TITL Grand Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Author of Or Yesha, son-in-law of the Zera Kodesh
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ropshitz is the name of a Hasidic dynasty, or rabbinical family and group who are descendants of Rabbi Naftali Zvi Horowitz of Ropshitz (1760-1827). Ropshitz is the name of a town in southern Poland known in Polish as Ropczyce.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many major rabbis are descendants of the Rebbes of Ropshitz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the offshoots of the Ropshitz dynasty are, the Dzikov, Glogov, Melitz, Stitshin, and Strizov dynasties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Today, Rabbi Chaim Meir Yechiel Rubin, the son of the Muzhayer Rebbe, styles himself as Ropshitzer Rebbe.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Rebbe Naftali Tzvi Horowitz of Ropshitz (1760-1827), son of Rabbi Mendl of Linsk
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Rebbe Eliezer Horowitz of Dzhikov (d. 1860), son of Rebbe Naftali Tzvi
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Rebbe Yaakov Horowitz ABD Kolbasov and Melitz (d.1839), son of Rebbe Naftali Tzvi
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Rebbe Avraham Chayim Horowitz of Linsk (d. 1831), son of Rebbe Naftali Tzvi
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Rebbe Asher Yeshayahu Rubin of Ropshitz (d.1855), son-in-law of Rebbe Naftali Tzvi
2 CONT
2 CONT                 + Rebbe Menashe Rubin of Ropshitz (d. 1861), son of Rebbe Asher Yeshayahu
2 CONT
2 CONT                       # Rabbi Reuven Horowitz ABD Dembitz, son-in-law of Rebbe Menashe
2 CONT
2 CONT                 + Rabbi Aharon Rubin of Rymanow (d. 1857), son of Rebbe Asher Yeshayahu
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ropshitz_(Hasidic_dynasty)
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebbe Asher Yeshaya Rubin of Ropshitz (c. 1777 – 1845), son-in-law of Rebbe Naftali Tzvi, known as Reb Osher'l. He succeeded his father-in-law as rabbi and rebbe of Ropshitz. His teachings were published in Or yeshaʻ (אור ישע) (Lv
2 CONC iv, 1876).
