2 CONT #Générale##Générale##Générale##Générale#Abraham Mendelssohn:Second son of MosesMendelssohn     ; bornat BerlinDec. 10, 1776     ; died there Nov. 19,1835     ; father of Felix Mendelssohn-Bartholdy. In 1803 he became cashier in Fo
2 CONC ulds' banking-house at Paris     ; but a year later he returned to Hamburg and went into partnershipwith his brother Joseph. Atthe same timehe married Leah Salomon, a granddaughter of Daniel Itzig,and was persuaded by hisbrother-i
2 CONC n-law,who at baptism had adopted thename of Bartholdy, to call himself "Mendelssohn-Bartholdy." During the siege of Hamburg by theFrench, Abraham and his brother were obligedto leave thecity on a foggy night secretly and in disgui
2 CONC se. They wentto Berlin and founded th
2 CONT ere the bank
2 CONT ing firm of Mendelssohn & Co., from which Abr
2 CONT a
2 CONT ham laterretired. In the year 1813 he equipped severalvolunteers at his own expense, and inrecognition of his efforts for the public welfare he waselected to the municipal council of Berlin.[bs.MalkaCahen.FTW]
2 CONT
