1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Writer of the book Gur Aryeh Yehuda:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=19747&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT the book was published in 1826-1827. On page 2 he mentions his wife who passed away and it seems he was quite old then.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=36783&st=&pgnum=93
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=6392&st=&pgnum=86
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=5704&pgnum=275
2 CONT
2 CONT Here he is giving a Hascama at the beginning of 1814: http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=5761&pgnum=6
2 CONT
2 CONT In ענף עץ אבות it says that his wife was the daughter of Rabbi Yosef Teomim from Ostravtza and not him
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Aryeh (Judah) Lieb Teomim of Brody married Michele, daughter of Samuel Bick, also of Brody. His first wife died, having no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aryeh was A.B.D. of Brody from 1815, on the death of Meir Kristianpoller, author of Gur Arey Yehuda, published in Zolkiew, 1827. He is mentioned in the Responsa of R' Haim Cohen Chelek.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also wrote Ayelet Ahavim, Zolkiew in 1822, and Ya'elat Chein, Zolkiew 1822. Aryeh became A.B.D. Lyzhansk when only fifteen years old and the time of the Noam Elimelech, the Chassidic leader of the community. They quarreled cons
2 CONC tantly.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his first wife, he remarried Michele who was divorced from her first husband, R Meshullam Igra of Tymenitsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (1990) Volume 1, page 251, G 9.1
2 CONT Pam Karp
2 CONT
2 CONT By Moshe Kutten: Date of birth from Yivo - https://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/teomim-aryeh-leib Wife - Michal daughter of Shmuel Bick of Brody, from an article by Meir Wender in the memorial book Ner Tamid leBrody (Israel, 1994)
2 CONC , page 86. The book was translated to English and can be found on Jewishgen.org web site ( https://www.jewishgen.org/Yizkor/brody/brody.html )
