1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Freydl [Rosina-Perl] (Teomim-Zwillinger) Zwillinger, dau of R’ Isaac Teomim-Zwillinger and wife of Abraham Teomim-Zwillinger, was born in Lissa, Poland, 1757.  She died in household #24, Holesov, on 19 December 183
2 CONC 5, age 78 years.  Her cause of death is given as "fever".  She is also seen as  "Ciperl", "Paula", and as "Freydl".  She is sometimes listed as "Freydl Isaak” and as “Paula Isaak" (Freydl / Paula, daughter of Isaak).
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of seven children, of whom only two — Channa (Zwillinger) Tauber (1777-1826) and Joseph Zwillinger (1791-1830) — lived to adulthood.  Both predeceased her.  When she died in December 1835, her eldest grandson, M
2 CONC arkus Tauber alias Zwillinger (b. 1797), was residing in House No. 24 and caring for her.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1830, “wittwe Fradl” [Zwillinger] is listed as the “previous occupant” of household #24.d -- Holesov, 1830:  [household #24.d] ZWILLINGER, Markus – previous occupant:  “Fraidl, wittwe”.
