1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was the daughter of R' Isaac Teomim-Zwillinger (c1726-c1791) of Lissa and his wife Chaja [Anna] (1726-1792).  Her marriage record in 1794 calls her “Jachwid ZWILLINGER”, but, in the birth records of her childre
2 CONC n, she is alternately identified as “Jachwid Isak” or as “Zartl Isak”.  Her death record refers to her as “Anna Frankl”, but that is the only time she is seen by that name — likely an error.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the witnesses to her 1794 marriage was her brother-in-law, Abraham Zwillinger (1754-1824), husband of her sister, Freydl (Zwillinger) Zwillinger (1757-1835).  Because both of her parents were deceased by 1794, she appears t
2 CONC o have been living in Abraham and Freydl’s household.
