2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Pińczów during the Holocaust
2 CONT
2 CONT Pińczów was destroyed by Germans in September 1939 and almost all Jews, who had accounted for about 70% of the town's population, were killed or sent to extermination camps. Most Pińczów's Jews were dead in the death camp Treblink
2 CONC a. The Jewish cemetery was also destroyed. Some Jews of Pińczów survived the Holocaust by hiding in nearby forests. Some, though not many, were hidden by Polish farmers until the end of the war.
