1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Shmuel Pessah is on the Montefiore census of 1839 with his family:
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Tzvi Age 43 Status Married, Male Title Rav Place of Birth Vilnius, Lithuania Year of Arrival 1818 Occupation studies Torah & worker Status Married, Female Name Shmuel Pessah Age 15 Status Son, Male Name Pesa Yehudit Age 4 Sta
2 CONC tus Daughter, Female  http://www.montefiorecensuses.org/search/scans/11730044.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1855 census, his daughter Leyla is Lea Malka b 1849:
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Shmuel Pesah Age 31 Status Married, Male Place of Birth Safed, Eretz Israel Occupation Beadle Name Tcherna Status Married, Female Name Lea Malka Age 6 Status Daughter, Female
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1849, she's listed as Haya: 	
2 CONT Name Shmuel Pesah Age 25 Status Married, Male Place of Birth Safed, Eretz Israel Occupation Beadle of Bikur Holim Name Haya Status Daughter, Female Name Tcherne Status Married, Female
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1866, he was 40 yrs old, married to Cerna and the father of Joseph and Jacob and a daughter Yocheved. He was the shamash (beadle) of the 'small synagogue', Bikur Holim,  and spent his time studying Torah, as did most of the res
2 CONC idents of Hevron. He is listed in the census of Chabad (Lubavitcher) Hassidim in Hevron. No occupation is listed and he is considered 'poor'. Name is spelled a variety of ways Meisels or Meiseles. Listed in the 1866 and 1875 Monte
2 CONC fiore census of Hebron. In 1875 he is listed again, but only two children are listed, Jacob and Yocheved. No occupation is listed and he is considered 'poor' (again, like most residents).
