1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''אדל אשכנזי''' (קרי: אוֹדֶל או אִידְל; ה'ת"ף – ה'תקמ"ז)[1], הייתה בתו של הבעל שם טוב, אבי תנועת החסידות. מעט ידוע בוודאות על קורות חייה, אך היא הפכה לדמות חשובה באגדות החסידים.
2 CONT
2 CONT בשבחי הבעש"ט מסופר כי לפני פטירתו, אמר אביה ש"לקח את נשמתה מן התורה, מן הפסוק הכתוב אש דת למו (דברים, לג, ב)"
2 CONT
2 CONT Adel Ashkenazi (literally: Odel or Ichal;)[1] was the daughter of the Baal Shem Tov, the father of the Hasidic movement. Little is known
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no certainty about her life story, but she became an important figure in Hasidic legends.
2 CONT
2 CONT In praise of the Baal Shem Tov, it is said that before his passing, her father said that "he took her soul from the Torah, from the verse written, 'A fire of righteousness for them' (Deuteronomy 33:2)
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Adil, was the only daughter of Rabbi Yisroel, the Baal Shem tov, and his wife, Chana chabad ea Rochel.  Her father said that he took the name ADiL from the verse in the Torah which concludes with the words, "Esh Dat Lamo" (Deutero
2 CONC nomy 33.2).
2 CONT
2 CONT Adil was known for her righteousness and was blessed with ruach hakodesh.  The Baal Shem Tov thought very highly of his daughter and treated her as one o fhis holy disciples.  Adil accompanied her father on his attempted pilgrimag
2 CONC e to the Holy Land.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Adil was married to Rabbi Yechiel Ashkenazi, who was known as the Daitchel ---coming from Germany.  together they had three famous children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT - Rabbi Moshe Chaim Ephraim of Sudylkov, author of the Degel Machane Ephraim,
2 CONT
2 CONT - Rabbi Baruch of Medzeboz, author of Butzina DeNehora, and
2 CONT
2 CONT - Feiga, Rabbi Nachman of Breslov's mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reb. Nachman of Breslov once said, "My grandmother, Adil, always yearned for G-ed.  She constantly looked for ways to please her Creator.".
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baal_Shem_Tov_family_tree
2 CONT --------------------
