1 NAME Edel Riwka /Scheuer/
2 GIVN Edel Riwka
2 SURN Scheuer
2 _MARNM Kauffmann
2 NICK Rifke
2 NICK Egid Scheuer
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Jüdischer Friedhof Schwarzrheindorf
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 C2, 79
3 CITY Bonn
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 MAY 1782
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bonn
3 STAE North Rhine-Westphalia
3 CTRY Germany
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edel died 11 May 1782 and is buried in Bonn/Schwarzrheindorf C2, 79 per Brocke Bonn pg. 185.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob bn Moses Kauffman's wife was (Rifke) Edel bt Reuven Scheuer seGal. This is the Reuven Scheuer whose house, the goldenes Moersel, burned at Chanukah 1754. Edel's mother was already dead at that time. Here is Reuven on Geni: h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Reuven-Beyfuss-Scheuer/6000000018587571401?through=6000000014119479666 and I have enormous amounts of data on him, his (correct) ancestors, and his descendants, in spite of the fact that he is the Number
2 CONC  One Winner in the Improbable Marriages Contest. I've been working for 20 years on his two or three wives, in an attempt to get them straight, with only minimal luck so far. Perhaps this will revive my zeal. But the good news is t
2 CONC hat his first wife, Elle HO 5918 =4 V 1743 bt Meir Kulp, is absolutely fine and well-documented. Thank goodness – because she is Edel's mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edel died 11 May 1782 and is buried in Bonn/Schwarzrheindorf C2, 79 per Brocke Bonn pg. 185.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several inaccuracies and iffy items in Schulte contribute to this problem. The first is that the daughter of Jacob and Edel, Elle (named for Edel's mother), who died 21 Oct 1799 and is buried in Bonn/Schwarzrheindorf C2, 53 per Br
2 CONC ocke Bonn pg. 236, is shown in Schulte as Jacob's sister, rather than his daughter. Brocke corrects this. Schulte gives a marriage year for Jacob and Edel of 1753. This seems extremely late, and is, in fact, incorrect. Elle was bo
2 CONC rn in 1743, as she is listed as age 56 when she dies in 1799. So this places Edel's birth year in a range between 1698 (the year of the death of her great-grandmother, Edel, wife of Feibisch Scheuer  - Reuven and Elle were not mar
2 CONC ried yet at that point anyway) and 1728, assuming that she did not give birth to her daughter Elle before age 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT In any case, a marriage year for Jacob and Edel of about 1742 would seem likely, and if the source of the name "Meir Loeb Goldschmidt of Frankfurt" is some record actually pertaining to the marriage contract, it could be explained
2 CONC  as being a relative in Frankfurt who was facilitating the matter while Reuven Scheuer was dealing with problems at home (his wife may have been ill, as she died the following year). Reuven did, in fact, have an uncle, Meir (bn Jo
2 CONC sef) Goldschmidt Kassel seGal, husband of Reuven's aunt Bluemle bt Feibisch Scheuer. Did his name get on the marriage contract in a way that was mistaken for the bride's father's name?
2 CONT
2 CONT Or an easier solution would be that what Schulte had seen was something relating to Jacob and Edel's SON: Meir Loeb, which claimed he was "named after his grandfather", and that this was misinterpreted. He was, presumably, named f
2 CONC or Edel's grandfather, Meir Kulp, who was the son of a Juda (although in the Kulp family Juda was not necessarily Loeb).  But more important than either of these theories is the point that Schulte gives Jacob an incorrect death da
2 CONC te in addition to (what we now see is) the incorrect marriage year. So was he actually looking at a different man – one whose wife was a daughter of Meir Loeb Goldschmidt and whom he married in 1753? If so, who was he? I don't see
2 CONC  anyone with that death date (3 March 1779) in Brocke Bonn, but perhaps he died elsewhere.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to Elle, there is also at least one more child for Jacob and Edel who does not show on Geni: (Sara) Jentche =30 IX 1797 HO 4259 bt Jacob Neuwied, who married her cousin, Isaac Beyfus Scheuer seGal (=12 XI 1827 at age 8
2 CONC 5) son of Reuven's brother Moses Scheuer by Hendel Arnstein.
2 CONT
2 CONT That’s all for now. Thanks again. I love working with the fascinating Scheuer family!
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy
