1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Deutschland, ausgewählte evangelische Kirchenbücher 1500-1971," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QP23-N5NK : 27 October 2021), Isaac Michael Speÿer in entry for Isaac Speÿer, 12 Jan 
2 CONC 1823; images digitized and records extracted by Ancestry; citing Marriage, Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preußen, Deutschland, Frankfurt, German Lutheran Collection, various parishes, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "From 1781 he was the Imperial Court Agent with responsibility for supplying munitions to and raising money for the German Emperor and his Minister Metternich. He died in Offenbach on 4 December 1807. He has accumulated 420,000 gu
2 CONC ilders, which was the largest fortune so far possessed by any Frankfurt Jew. Its main source had been profits from exchange broking and the supplying of military equipment during the French invasion. At this point even Mayer Amsch
2 CONC el Rothschild's fortune only amounted to 60,000 guilders and at no point in his lifetime did his fortune equal even half as much as that of Isaak [b] Michael Speyer." (Dietz, Alexander. The Jewish Community of Frankfurt. Vamderher
2 CONC  Publications. Cornwall: 1988. p, 334)
