0 @N6000000004339667748@ NOTE FROM JEWISH ENCYCLOPEDIA:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1727-1792 (4 Iyar 5552) JOSEPH TEOMIM
1 CONT
1 CONT Rabbi, halachic authority, and teacher. Teomim composed the Pri Migadim
1 CONT (Sweet Fruits), one of the most comprehensive commentaries on the Shulchan
1 CONT Aruch. Originally intended as a super-commentary on the Shach and Taz (on the Shulchan Aruch), he actually solved problems raised by himself. His work, accepted by all Orthodox Jews (Ashkenazic, Sephardic, Hasidic), is based on a 
1 CONC systematic analysis of previous commentators (Rishonim) upon whom the commentators based themselves. At the same time he emphasized that his decisions are not to be taken as definitive halachah. He was an authority on grammar as w
1 CONC ell as the Talmud, and understood rudimentary logic. He also authored a commentary on the Torah entitled Rav Peninim (Many Pearls). In addition he wrote Porat Yosef and Rosh Yosef novellae to various talmudic tractates.
