1 CONT FRET
0 @N6000000002765656298@ NOTE
1 CONT In the wake of Wolf Liepman, founder of the Westminster Synagogue, there had
1 CONT come over from Vienna to London his two nephews, the sons of Samuel
1 CONT Pressburg, the affluent Austrian banker and Government agent. One of this
1 CONT couple was to play a very important part in London life in his day. This was
1 CONT R. Leib Pressburg, to give him the Synagogue name, known in the outside
1 CONT world as Baron Lyon de Symons, of Great Prescott Street, Goodman's Fields,
1 CONT and Lower Tooting. A wealthy diamond-merchant, he was active at quite an
1 CONT early date in the affairs of the Great Synagogue, and his exertions in 1785
1 CONT in conjunction with Rabbi Tevele Schiff, on behalf of a Jewish boy who had
1 CONT got into trouble, show clearly that he enjoyed valuable society connexions
1 CONT and influence. Indeed, "Mr. de Simon", with his uncle Wolf Liepman, Mr.
1 CONT (Aaron?) Franks and Mr. Moses Zunz, "at Mr. Salter's the grocer corner, in
1 CONT Pulteny Street", together with Mr. d'Almeida in Took's Court, Chancery Lane,
1 CONT and an Italian Jewish 'cellist named Graziani, were among the persons whose
1 CONT names Mozart's father noted down as useful connexions when he brought his
1 CONT son to London in 1764. Lyon de Symons married a daughter of Aaron
1 CONT Goldsmid's, served in all the executive offices of the Great Synagogue, and
1 CONT for some years before his death in 1814 was one of the outstanding
1 CONT characters of London Jewry. With his Continental experience and his passion
1 CONT for organisation, he took a leading part in many of the reforms which were
1 CONT to take place in these years.
0 @N6000000007008515280@ NOTE
1 CONT Simon Michael 1656-1719 und sein Sohn Michael Lazar 1687-1756 - sie waren
1 CONT angesehene Hoffaktoren in Pressburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT Michael married Helene [Levia]Austerlitz 1687-1746 die wird oft in Akten nur
1 CONT alse die Schone  Judin bezeichnet.
1 CONT
1 CONT It shows the brother of Michael Lazar as Samuel Michael 1696- 1762 who
1 CONT married Fratia Liebmann -their son was Low [with umlaut] Simon, 1741-1814,
1 CONT who married Polly Goldsmith. Low Simon war in siener Jugend en Mitgrunder
1 CONT der Wiener Chevra Kadisha und in Jahre 1763 nach England ubersiedelt.
1 CONT Anderte sein name auf Lyon de Symons .
1 CONT
1 CONT He had one son Aaron and five daughters - who married
